MiniLaTeX is a no-setup subset of \LaTeX\ that can be rendered on
the fly to \HTML. One can use it to build web apps with true \HTML\ display
viewable on any device from smart phone to tablet to desktop.
Typesetting occurs in real time, and error messages are displayed
in-line in the rendered text. MiniLaTeX documents can be exported to
standard \LaTeX.

We describe (a) MiniLaTeX the language, (b)~the main features of the
document management application \tbsurl{minilatex.lamdera.app}, and (c)
some of the technical work required to implement an on-the-fly
\LaTeX-to-\HTML\ compiler.

A video  version  of  this  paper is at \url{https://youtu.be/TAIYpCc3VV0}.
The document was originally written in MiniLaTeX and is
available at \tbsurl{minilatex.lamdera.app/g/22}.
